    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "And particularly with the Republican majority, I mean, you have to give Nancy Pelosi credit one way or another. She kept her caucus in line. And I don't know how she did it. I mean, I generally have sat down with some of my Democratic colleagues in the last few days and asked, how did she do it? But for whatever reason, Republicans are more political entrepreneurs. They're more willing to take a stand against their own party, against their own leadership. And I think we all recognize that. We saw that under John Boehner. We saw it under Paul Ryan. And it's certainly going to be true under Kevin McCarthy. The question you have, though, Jake, is have we weakened the speakership to the point where it is an already difficult job as impossible. And that's something that many of us have worried about. I got to tell you, I don't think that we have.",
